{
  "reports": [
    {
      "title": "20260908 Synthetic Series 07: Feeder F-3 Distribution Automation Loop Misoperation During Storm Restoration",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "At 14:23, a 94-km/h storm gust pushed a willow branch into Synthetic Substation S-07 feeder F-3, creating a phase A-to-ground fault.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The loop-transfer timer in feeder F-3 was set to 720 milliseconds, far shorter than the loop's 1.35-second SCADA scan interval.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The automation logic did not require the recloser's lockout confirmation before classifying fault impulses in the loop evaluation.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Because storm restoration mode remained active, the loop's pickup threshold was reduced from 440 amperes to 220 amperes at 13:42.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The scheme classified events using only the number of overcurrent pulses and did not compare phase-angle measurements from both feeder ends.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "At 14:23:01, the source breaker at Synthetic Substation S-07 tripped after 2.8 cycles because fault current reached 1,450 amperes.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [0]
        },
        {
          "text": "The breaker's automatic reclose after 45 cycles reenergized the unchanged tree fault, causing a second relay trip.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [5]
        },
        {
          "text": "Because the 720-millisecond timer expired before the lockout message, the controller counted the two current pulses as separate zones.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [6, 1, 2]
        },
        {
          "text": "Misclassifying the pulses as a source-loss event, the loop automation then issued a close command to tie switch TS-118.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [7, 3, 4]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 14:23:47, tie switch TS-118 closed, thereby connecting intact feeder F-9 to the still-faulted section of feeder F-3.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "The F-9 relay tripped after 302 milliseconds due to backfeed through TS-118; this trip was not caused by lightning, as surge arresters logged no operation.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The automated loop then suppressed automatic reclosing on F-9 because it detected a false islanding condition.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [10]
        },
        {
          "text": "This left the F-3 breaker in lockout while the faulted pole P-38 remained connected through the upstream sectionalizer.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [6]
        },
        {
          "text": "All seven downstream load groups on feeder F-3, totaling 394 customers, were deenergized for at least fifteen minutes.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "Feeder F-9 lost its healthy segment, interrupting 214 homes and delaying full restoration by 21 minutes past the 38-minute design target.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [10, 13]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 14:29, the dispatcher remotely opened tie switch TS-118 using SCADA override after noticing the second overcurrent indication.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [14, 10]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 14:43, a crew at pole P-38 manually opened sectionalizer F3-S21, isolating the faulted branch from the healthy feeder.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [15]
        },
        {
          "text": "Workers closed source breaker and tie switch TS-118 after verifying phase rotation, restoring all 214 homes and F-3 loads by 15:04.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [16]
        },
        {
          "text": "Engineering changed the timer from 720 milliseconds to 1.9 seconds and required a confirmed lockout state before any transfer.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [17]
        },
        {
          "text": "Engineering also added a phase-angle comparison and a storm-mode veto of pulse-count decisions to prevent recurrence of this loop misoperation.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [18]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Synthetic T-19 Feeder R-2 False Source-Loss Detection and Tie Closure During Storm Restoration in Synthetic Series 07",
      "core_units": [
        {
          "text": "At 22:18, gusty rain pushed an oak branch across feeder R-2 at Synthetic Substation T-19, creating a B-phase-to-ground fault at pole 112.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Feeder R-2's loop configuration file T19-2026 maps neutral-current channels in reverse, making residual readings unreliable when a switch is opened.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The source-loss timer is set to 250 milliseconds, which is shorter than the 1.3-second period of balanced residual decay after a switching event.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "In storm restoration mode, the controller disables the undervoltage check that would confirm the feeder is deenergized below 60 volts.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The enable map omitted the remote sectionalizer's acknowledgment bit, so the controller lacks actual open-close confirmation from R2-S5.",
          "role": "root_cause",
          "causal_predecessors": []
        },
        {
          "text": "At 22:19, the R-2 source breaker tripped to lockout after 1.6 cycles because the phase fault current reached 2,010 amperes.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [0]
        },
        {
          "text": "The breaker trip deenergized feeder R-2, causing capacitor bank CB-19 to discharge a 700-ampere pulse through the residual current transformer for 300 milliseconds.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [5]
        },
        {
          "text": "Because the pulse duration of 300 ms exceeded the faulty 250-millisecond source-loss timer, the controller concluded that feeder R-2 had lost source.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [6, 2, 3]
        },
        {
          "text": "Thus, the loop automation issued a close command to tie switch N-4 and did not wait for sectionalizer R2-S5 to report open.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [7, 1, 4]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 22:23, tie switch N-4 closed because of the erroneous close command, connecting the healthy feeder R-1 to the faulted pole-112 branch.",
          "role": "trigger_event",
          "causal_predecessors": [8]
        },
        {
          "text": "Feeder R-1's relay operated after 260 milliseconds due to backfeed through the closed tie; there was no fault on feeder R-1 itself.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [9]
        },
        {
          "text": "The automation loop then blocked further operations for 5 minutes after it misinterpreted the R-1 trip as a parallel-source condition.",
          "role": "propagation_or_response",
          "causal_predecessors": [10]
        },
        {
          "text": "The false source-loss declaration prevented the sectionalizer R2-S5 from isolating the pole-112 fault before the tie closure.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [7, 8]
        },
        {
          "text": "This misoperation left 173 customers on the healthy segment of feeder R-1 deenergized for 32 minutes.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [10]
        },
        {
          "text": "Because the pole-112 branch stayed connected, feeder R-2's outage expanded to 440 customers on the two downstream laterals.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [12]
        },
        {
          "text": "Automatic restoration remained blocked until 23:05, adding 22 minutes to the 35-minute storm restoration target.",
          "role": "impact",
          "causal_predecessors": [11]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 22:34, dispatchers remotely opened tie switch N-4 and closed the R-1 source breaker, restoring all healthy R-1 customers.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [13]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 22:47, ground personnel at pole 112 manually opened the S-19 lateral disconnect, isolating the damaged branch.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [16]
        },
        {
          "text": "At 22:55, operators closed the R-2 source breaker, restoring all intact loads and leaving only the isolated S-19 lateral deenergized.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [17]
        },
        {
          "text": "Engineering set the source-loss timer to 1.5 seconds, corrected the enable map, and reenabled the undervoltage check after the storm.",
          "role": "mitigation",
          "causal_predecessors": [18]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
